## Context
__PROJECT_NAME__ is built partly by coding agents. For new work to stay
consistent with earlier choices, those choices and their rationale must be
written down where an agent will read them before implementing.

## Decision
We record significant architecture and technical decisions as ADRs in
`docs/03-decisions/`, one file per decision, using `_template.md`. ADRs are
immutable once `Accepted`: to change course we add a new ADR and mark the old one
`Superseded by ADR-XXXX` rather than editing its content. Numbering is sequential
(`0001`, `0002`, …).

## Alternatives considered
- **No written decisions** — rejected: agents re-litigate settled choices and
  drift from the architecture.
- **Decisions only in commit messages / PRs** — rejected: not discoverable at
  implementation time and easily lost.

## Consequences
- A decision that affects architecture (new dependency, new pattern, new service,
  changed boundary) SHOULD have an ADR, ideally written at planning time as
  `Proposed` and promoted to `Accepted` before implementation.
- Agents MUST check `03-decisions/` for relevant ADRs (by tag) before proposing a
  design, and MUST NOT silently reverse an `Accepted` ADR.
